 "title": "Identity Fights When You Become Disciplined",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator claims that when you decide to become disciplined, your identity fights you using smart strategies like procrastination, perfectionism, and busy work. When you notice these strategies happening, you should call them out in the moment.",
 "key_points": [
  "Your identity will fight back when you try to become disciplined.",
  "It uses strategies such as overthinking, overwhelm, procrastination, negative self-talk, self-doubt, perfectionism, comparison, distraction, busy work, endless research, and waiting for the perfect time.",
  "Busy work means doing all the little things while never doing the big thing.",
  "When you notice one of these strategies running, name it as it happens (e.g., \"Oh, I am procrastinating.\").",
  "Recognize that these are strategies of the identity, not who you fundamentally are."
 ],
 "content": "The creator explains that the second you decide to become disciplined, \"your identity is going to fight you.\" He claims it does not just walk up and say it does not want you to change; instead, it uses smart strategies. These strategies include overthinking, overwhelm, procrastination, negative self-talk, self-doubt, perfectionism, comparison, distraction, busy work (where you do all the little things but never the big thing), endless research and consumption, and waiting for the perfect time. The creator advises that when you notice one of these strategies is running, you should say what is happening when it is happening. For example, you can say, \"Oh, I am procrastinating.\" By doing this, you recognize it as \"a strategy of the identity\" rather than defining yourself by it.",
